NAME
    groupadd - create a group (root only)

SYNOPSIS
    groupadd <name> [-g <gid>]

DESCRIPTION
    Adds a group to /etc/group (format: name:gid:members). ROOT ONLY. The gid is
    the given -g value or the next free id at/above 1000.

    Groups here use a PRIMARY-GID model: a task carries one kernel-owned gid, and
    "putting a user in a group" means setting that user's primary gid (see
    usermod). The members list is recorded but not yet enforced - full
    supplementary-group membership needs the kernel identity to carry a group
    list, a later step.

EXAMPLES
    # groupadd staff
    groupadd: created group staff

SEE ALSO
    usermod, useradd, id
